// A wildcard import of a module that declares macros overloaded by repeating
// the name: each use in the importer picks among the whole set by its argument,
// so the importer is given every macro of the name, not the first alone. A
// public macro's body in the imported module uses a private overloaded pair,
// and that body expands here, so the importer gets that whole pair too.
//
// It compiles rather than runs, as module_imports_macro does: the imported
// module's bodies are never generated here. The IR check in cases.toml says
// which body each use expanded.
//
// The imported module is modulemacro_overload.cone.

mod module_imports_macro_overload;

import modulemacro_overload use *;

fn imports() i64 {
  bump(pick(1i64)) + bump(pick(true)) + bump(outer(7i64))
}
